# order.txt  --  optional. COPY this file to "order.txt" to use it. Copy, not
# rename: the installer build ships this example, so moving it breaks the build.
#
# When order.txt exists, the merger follows it exactly instead of just
# grabbing everything in .\input alphabetically. One source per line,
# top to bottom = the page order in the finished document.
#
# Sources can be PDFs, images (jpg, png, gif, bmp, tif, tiff, webp), Word
# documents (docx, doc, docm, rtf, odt) or spreadsheets (xlsx, xlsm, xls, csv,
# ods). Each image becomes one page; a multi-page TIFF becomes several. Word
# documents and spreadsheets are converted to PDF automatically, and their page
# ranges follow the converted document.
#
# Paths are looked up in .\input first, so a bare file name is enough.
# Absolute paths (C:\Users\...\file.pdf) work too.
#
# Add page ranges after a colon to pick pages:
#     1        a single page
#     2-5      a range, inclusive
#     7-       page 7 to the end
#     -4       start through page 4
#     all      every page (same as leaving it off)
#     1-3,7,10-   combine with commas, no spaces
#
# Put ! in front to REMOVE pages instead of picking them:
#     !7       every page except page 7
#     !2-4     every page except 2, 3 and 4
#     !1,3,5   drop those three, keep the rest
# (~ means the same as !, e.g. ~7)
#
# A pick-list can also reorder and repeat pages (3,1,1). An exclusion always
# keeps the surviving pages in their original order.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored, blank lines are ignored.
# The same file can appear as many times as you like.

cover.jpg
letter.docx
budget.xlsx
report.pdf:1-3,7
scan.pdf:!2
signed page.png
appendix.pdf:5-
C:\Users\you\Pictures\receipt.tiff:2
